       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day (and some institutions cap at 3 g/day). It risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options, depending on what you intended:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), a common standard regimen.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day).\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day), the maximum for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function.\n- **3000 mg/day total**, which may be what you meant. That would be 1000 mg three times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want the 3000 mg three-times-daily order, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
